// Q-171 A route that gives an `http.*` or file error sends the visitor its text: an internal address with its key, a path on the server. The log has no text at all. Q-161's fix covers `db:` values only
// mode: serve
// get: /billing
// get: /keys
// open-when: {"error":"http:
// open-when: {"error":"read_file:
// fixed-when: internal error
// From FEEDBACK21.md §Q-171 (found on c59890e).

route GET /billing = http.get("http://127.0.0.1:1/internal/billing?key=abc")
route GET /keys = read_file("/srv/app/secrets/keys.json")
